1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,810
A lightning bolt five times hotter

2
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:03,590
than the sun's surface just hit

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,230
the plane Gus is on, and

4
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:06,530
all he lost is his nap.

5
00:00:06,574 --> 00:00:08,254
It's nine at night, two miles

6
00:00:08,264 --> 00:00:09,494
up in a storm cloud, and

7
00:00:09,504 --> 00:00:10,334
Gus is asleep.

8
00:00:10,388 --> 00:00:10,698
Bang.

9
00:00:10,708 --> 00:00:11,598
A white flash.

10
00:00:11,608 --> 00:00:12,698
His wife screams.

11
00:00:12,938 --> 00:00:14,578
His neighbor throws both hands up.

12
00:00:14,632 --> 00:00:16,102
That bolt carries two thousand

13
00:00:16,112 --> 00:00:17,572
times the current that blows the

14
00:00:17,582 --> 00:00:18,702
fuse in his kitchen.

15
00:00:18,756 --> 00:00:19,346
But wait.

16
00:00:19,356 --> 00:00:20,386
Nobody is hurt.

17
00:00:20,396 --> 00:00:21,506
So where did it all go?

18
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,320
You see, electricity is lazy.

19
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:24,980
It takes the easy road, and

20
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:26,540
nothing is easier than metal.

21
00:00:26,594 --> 00:00:28,484
The plane's skin is aluminum, no

22
00:00:28,494 --> 00:00:29,434
thicker than a dime.

23
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:30,518
So the bolt lands on the

24
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:32,788
nose, runs along the outside, and

25
00:00:32,798 --> 00:00:33,848
jumps off the tail.

26
00:00:33,892 --> 00:00:35,422
Ever stand under an umbrella in

27
00:00:35,432 --> 00:00:36,012
the rain?

28
00:00:36,292 --> 00:00:37,832
The water runs around you, and

29
00:00:37,842 --> 00:00:38,672
you stay dry.

30
00:00:38,716 --> 00:00:39,906
Pushing all of it from nose

31
00:00:39,916 --> 00:00:41,276
to tail takes only a few

32
00:00:41,286 --> 00:00:41,866
volts.

33
00:00:42,116 --> 00:00:43,466
Less than a wall socket.

34
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:44,600
And it's no accident.

35
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:46,660
Every airliner gets hit about once

36
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:47,090
a year.

37
00:00:47,134 --> 00:00:48,654
Nine times out of ten, the

38
00:00:48,664 --> 00:00:50,474
plane sets the bolt off itself.

39
00:00:50,518 --> 00:00:51,978
Luckily, the lightning can't get

40
00:00:51,988 --> 00:00:52,568
to Gus.

41
00:00:52,622 --> 00:00:54,702
Unluckily, cabin air is bone dry,

42
00:00:54,912 --> 00:00:56,402
the floor is carpet, and Gus

43
00:00:56,412 --> 00:00:57,272
wears slippers.

44
00:00:57,326 --> 00:00:58,836
He shuffles to the bathroom and

45
00:00:58,846 --> 00:00:59,916
reaches for the knob.

46
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:00,240
Zap.

47
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,940
That tiny spark is three thousand

48
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:02,440
volts.

49
00:01:02,494 --> 00:01:03,874
The lightning never touched him.

50
00:01:04,054 --> 00:01:05,274
The doorknob did.
